### 29. Create lists beyond the limit of 50 -> 201 Created until the member has 50, then 409 Conflict
### NOT SCRIPTABLE end to end: a .http file cannot loop. Send this request again and again; each run uses a fresh
### name ({{$uuid}}), so it creates one more list until the member has 50, then answers 409 with the type
### urn:recettes:problem:too-many-recipe-lists. RecipeListsIntegrationTest does it for real.
### CLEAN UP afterwards: the lists made here are not removed by request 35, and with 50 of them request 6 of the
### next run answers 409. List them with GET /lists and DELETE the ones called "Liste ...".
POST {{baseUrl}}/lists
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Liste {{$uuid}}",
  "emoji": "📚"
}

> {%
    client.test("Returns 201 until the limit, then 409 of type too-many-recipe-lists", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201 || response.status === 409, "Expected 201 or 409 but got " + response.status);
        if (response.status === 409) {
            client.assert(response.body.type === "urn:recettes:problem:too-many-recipe-lists", "Got type " + response.body.type);
        }
    });
%}

### 30. Put a 201st recipe in a full list -> 409 Conflict
### NOT SCRIPTABLE end to end: it needs a list holding 200 recipes. Set @fullListId to such a list (the integration
### test builds one) and @notInItRecipeId to a recipe that is not in it. The answer is 409 with the type
### urn:recettes:problem:recipe-list-full - and 204 for a recipe that IS already in the list, because nothing would
### be added.
@fullListId = replace-with-a-list-holding-200-recipes
@notInItRecipeId = replace-with-a-recipe-that-is-not-in-it
PUT {{baseUrl}}/lists/{{fullListId}}/recipes/{{notInItRecipeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}

> {%
    client.test("Returns 409 of type recipe-list-full (404 until the placeholders are replaced)", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409 || response.status === 404, "Expected 409 (or 404 for the placeholders) but got " + response.status);
        if (response.status === 409) {
            client.assert(response.body.type === "urn:recettes:problem:recipe-list-full", "Got type " + response.body.type);
        }
    });
%}

